@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pru-nouns`

-- Named cases for the tests. No rules and no directives: every figure here is a scenario
-- value chosen by the tester (a sum insured of 1,000,000,000 VND, premiums of 30,000,000),
-- not a figure from the document.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `Policies`

GIVEN sa   IS A NUMBER
      term IS A NUMBER
      eff  IS A DATE
      dob  IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The policy`
`a policy for` sa `over` term `years from` eff `on an insured born` dob MEANS
    `The policy` WITH
        `sum insured`                                  IS sa
        `chosen contract term in years`                IS term
        `effective date`                               IS eff
        `the insured's date of birth`                  IS dob
        `date the contract last ceased to be in force` IS NOTHING
        `date of the latest reinstatement`             IS NOTHING

-- The ordinary case: 1 billion VND, 10 years from 15 January 2026, an adult insured.
`the policy` MEANS `a policy for` 1_000_000_000 `over` 10 `years from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `on an insured born` (YMD 1990 6 1)

GIVEN sa   IS A NUMBER
      dob  IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the same policy for` sa `on an insured born` dob MEANS
    `a policy for` sa `over` 10 `years from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `on an insured born` dob

GIVEN ceased     IS A DATE
      reinstated IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the policy, lapsed on` ceased `and reinstated on` reinstated MEANS
    `The policy` WITH
        `sum insured`                                  IS 1_000_000_000
        `chosen contract term in years`                IS 10
        `effective date`                               IS YMD 2026 1 15
        `the insured's date of birth`                  IS YMD 1990 6 1
        `date the contract last ceased to be in force` IS JUST ceased
        `date of the latest reinstatement`             IS reinstated

§§ `Accounts and earlier payments`

GIVEN premiums IS A NUMBER
      sv       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      owed     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      medical  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `The accounts`
`accounts with premiums` premiums `surrender value` sv `debts` owed `medical costs` medical MEANS
    `The accounts` WITH
        `total premiums paid`                         IS premiums
        `total premiums paid up to the insured event` IS premiums
        `surrender value`                             IS sv
        `debts`                                       IS owed
        `medical examination and test costs`          IS medical

`the accounts` MEANS `accounts with premiums` 30_000_000 `surrender value` NOTHING `debts` NOTHING `medical costs` NOTHING

GIVEN x1 IS A NUMBER
      x2 IS A NUMBER
      x3 IS A NUMBER
      x4 IS A NUMBER
      x5 IS A NUMBER
      x6 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Benefits already paid`
`already paid: permanent injury` x1 `organ` x2 `fracture` x3 `burn` x4 `ambulance this year` x5 `injury benefits for this accident` x6 MEANS
    `Benefits already paid` WITH
        `permanent-injury benefit paid during the term`                IS x1
        `internal-organ benefit paid during the term`                  IS x2
        `fracture benefit paid during the term`                        IS x3
        `burn benefit paid during the term`                            IS x4
        `ambulance benefit paid in the contract year of the accident`  IS x5
        `injury benefits under Articles 8.2-8.5 paid for this accident` IS x6

`nothing paid yet` MEANS `already paid: permanent injury` 0 `organ` 0 `fracture` 0 `burn` 0 `ambulance this year` 0 `injury benefits for this accident` 0

§§ `Causes`

-- One helper per cause: the named cause has the given link, every other cause is unrelated.
GIVEN war IS A `A link to a cause`
      crime IS A `A link to a cause`
      concluded IS A BOOLEAN
      suicide IS A `A link to a cause`
      danger IS A `A link to a cause`
      substance IS A `A link to a cause`
      prescribed IS A BOOLEAN
      `influence caused it` IS A BOOLEAN
      drugs IS A `A link to a cause`
      drink IS A `A link to a cause`
      intent IS A `A link to a cause`
      several IS A BOOLEAN
      illness IS A `A link to a cause`
GIVETH A `The causes of the event`
`the causes` war crime concluded suicide danger substance prescribed `influence caused it` drugs drink intent several illness MEANS
    `The causes of the event` WITH
        `war, belligerent acts, rebellion, civil disorder or riot`             IS war
        `a crime of the policyholder, the insured or the claimant`            IS crime
        `a competent State authority concluded it was a crime`                IS concluded
        `suicide or self-inflicted injury of the insured`                     IS suicide
        `a dangerous activity of the insured`                                 IS danger
        `the influence of addictive substances, psychiatric drugs, alcohol, poison, gas, similar substances or narcotics` IS substance
        `the substance was prescribed by a Doctor`                            IS prescribed
        `the influence was the cause of the Accident`                         IS `influence caused it`
        `illegal use of narcotics or stimulants`                              IS drugs
        `driving with a blood alcohol level above the legal limit`            IS drink
        `an intentional act of the policyholder, the insured or the claimant` IS intent
        `the intentional act was that of one of several beneficiaries`        IS several
        `an illness (such as osteoporosis or a bone disease), or medical treatment` IS illness

`no excluded cause` MEANS `the causes` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it`

GIVEN l IS A `A link to a cause`
GIVETH A `The causes of the event`
`war, linked as` l MEANS `the causes` l `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it`

GIVEN l IS A `A link to a cause`
      concluded IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The causes of the event`
`a crime, linked as` l `concluded by an authority` concluded MEANS `the causes` `not related to it` l concluded `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it`

GIVEN l IS A `A link to a cause`
GIVETH A `The causes of the event`
`suicide or self-injury, linked as` l MEANS `the causes` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE l `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it`

GIVEN l IS A `A link to a cause`
GIVETH A `The causes of the event`
`a dangerous activity, linked as` l MEANS `the causes` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it` l `not related to it` FALSE FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it`

GIVEN l IS A `A link to a cause`
      rx IS A BOOLEAN
      caused IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The causes of the event`
`a substance, linked as` l `prescribed` rx `and the cause of the Accident` caused MEANS `the causes` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` l rx caused `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it`

GIVEN l IS A `A link to a cause`
      several IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The causes of the event`
`an intentional act, linked as` l `by one of several beneficiaries` several MEANS `the causes` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` l several `not related to it`

GIVEN l IS A `A link to a cause`
GIVETH A `The causes of the event`
`an illness or treatment, linked as` l MEANS `the causes` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE l

GIVEN l IS A `A link to a cause`
GIVETH A `The causes of the event`
`drink-driving, linked as` l MEANS `the causes` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it` `not related to it` `not related to it` FALSE FALSE `not related to it` l `not related to it` FALSE `not related to it`

§§ `Accidents and deaths`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      c IS A `The causes of the event`
GIVETH AN `An accident`
`an accident on` d `with` c MEANS
    `An accident` WITH
        `date of the accident`                                           IS d
        `caused by the impact of a sudden external force or object`      IS TRUE
        `involuntary and unintended`                                     IS TRUE
        `at a determinate time and place`                                IS TRUE
        `the sole and direct cause, unrelated to any other cause such as illness` IS TRUE
        `causes`                                                         IS c

-- An event that fails Article 1.16: it was not the sole cause (a heart attack at the wheel).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An accident`
`an event that was not the sole cause, on` d MEANS
    `An accident` WITH
        `date of the accident`                                           IS d
        `caused by the impact of a sudden external force or object`      IS TRUE
        `involuntary and unintended`                                     IS TRUE
        `at a determinate time and place`                                IS TRUE
        `the sole and direct cause, unrelated to any other cause such as illness` IS FALSE
        `causes`                                                         IS `no excluded cause`

-- The accident used throughout: 10 March 2027, no excluded cause.
`the accident` MEANS `an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` `no excluded cause`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      e IS A MAYBE `An accident`
      m IS A `A mode of travel at the time of death`
GIVETH A `A death of the insured`
`a death on` d `from` e `as` m MEANS
    `A death of the insured` WITH
        `date of death`            IS d
        `the event that caused it` IS e
        `mode of travel`           IS m

§§ `Medical facts`

`a Doctor` MEANS
    `A medical practitioner` WITH
        `a university degree in Western medicine or higher`       IS TRUE
        `lawfully licensed locally to examine, treat and operate` IS TRUE
        `relation to the parties`                                 IS `no such relation`

`the insured's brother, a doctor` MEANS
    `A medical practitioner` WITH
        `a university degree in Western medicine or higher`       IS TRUE
        `lawfully licensed locally to examine, treat and operate` IS TRUE
        `relation to the parties`                                 IS `an immediate family member of the policyholder or the insured`

GIVEN b IS A `A bone in the fracture table`
      d IS A DATE
      prev IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `A fracture`
`a fracture of` b `on` d `previously broken` prev MEANS
    `A fracture` WITH
        `the bone`                                            IS b
        `a complete break, not a hairline crack or greenstick fracture` IS TRUE
        `confirmed on X-ray, CT or MRI by`                    IS `a Doctor`
        `date of the fracture`                                IS d
        `date of the previous fracture of the same bone`      IS prev

GIVEN b IS A `A bone in the fracture table`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A fracture`
`a greenstick fracture of` b `on` d MEANS
    `A fracture` WITH
        `the bone`                                            IS b
        `a complete break, not a hairline crack or greenstick fracture` IS FALSE
        `confirmed on X-ray, CT or MRI by`                    IS `a Doctor`
        `date of the fracture`                                IS d
        `date of the previous fracture of the same bone`      IS NOTHING

GIVEN b IS A `A bone in the fracture table`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A fracture`
`a fracture of` b `on` d `confirmed only by the insured's brother` MEANS
    `A fracture` WITH
        `the bone`                                            IS b
        `a complete break, not a hairline crack or greenstick fracture` IS TRUE
        `confirmed on X-ray, CT or MRI by`                    IS `the insured's brother, a doctor`
        `date of the fracture`                                IS d
        `date of the previous fracture of the same bone`      IS NOTHING

GIVEN h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A head injury`
`a coma in hours of` h MEANS
    `A head injury` WITH
        `continuous coma, in hours`                                         IS h
        `Glasgow score of 6 or less throughout 96 hours of hospital treatment` IS h AT LEAST 96
        `needed life support`                                               IS TRUE
        `coma directly caused by alcohol, an addictive substance or illness` IS FALSE
        `depressed skull fracture`                                          IS FALSE
        `dural tear with acute subdural haematoma shown on CT or MRI`        IS FALSE
        `needed brain surgery`                                              IS FALSE
        `only a linear vault fracture or a skull-base fracture`             IS FALSE

GIVEN `linear only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A head injury`
`a depressed skull fracture with surgery, linear vault fracture only` `linear only` MEANS
    `A head injury` WITH
        `continuous coma, in hours`                                         IS 0
        `Glasgow score of 6 or less throughout 96 hours of hospital treatment` IS FALSE
        `needed life support`                                               IS FALSE
        `coma directly caused by alcohol, an addictive substance or illness` IS FALSE
        `depressed skull fracture`                                          IS TRUE
        `dural tear with acute subdural haematoma shown on CT or MRI`        IS TRUE
        `needed brain surgery`                                              IS TRUE
        `only a linear vault fracture or a skull-base fracture`             IS `linear only`

GIVEN third  IS A NUMBER
      second IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A burn`
`a burn of` third `percent at third degree and` second `percent at second degree` MEANS
    `A burn` WITH
        `percent of body skin area with third-degree burns`  IS third
        `percent of body skin area with second-degree burns` IS second

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of medical facility`
GIVETH A `A medical facility`
`a facility of kind` k MEANS
    `A medical facility` WITH
        `kind`                                                     IS k
        `established and operating under Vietnamese law to examine and treat patients` IS TRUE
        `inpatient treatment`                                      IS TRUE
        `operating 24/7 with licensed doctors, physicians and nurses` IS TRUE
        `managed by persons licensed by a competent authority`     IS TRUE
        `keeping and providing medical and financial records as the law requires` IS TRUE

GIVEN f  IS A `A medical facility`
      er IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A care unit`
`an intensive care unit in` f `which is an emergency room` er MEANS
    `A care unit` WITH
        `in`                                                       IS f
        `a post-operative room or an emergency room`               IS er
        `with inpatient accommodation`                             IS TRUE
        `set up for an intensive care and treatment programme`     IS TRUE
        `reserved for patients whose vital functions are threatened, needing a Doctor's monitoring` IS TRUE
        `equipped on site for immediate intervention`              IS TRUE

GIVEN u IS A MAYBE `A care unit`
      t IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The emergency treatment`
`treated overnight in` u `transferred` t MEANS
    `The emergency treatment` WITH
        `treated overnight in`            IS u
        `transferred to another hospital` IS t

GIVEN parts IS A MAYBE `A pair of body parts`
      paralysis IS A BOOLEAN
      capacity IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      onset IS A DATE
      cert IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A disability`
`a disability of` parts `by paralysis` paralysis `capacity lost` capacity `from` onset `certified` cert MEANS
    `A disability` WITH
        `loss or complete irrecoverable paralysis of`              IS parts
        `by paralysis`                                             IS paralysis
        `only a weakening of the limbs`                            IS FALSE
        `loss of working capacity, in percent`                     IS capacity
        `confirmed by a provincial-level or higher medical authority or assessment council` IS TRUE
        `date of the accident or of the definitive diagnosis`      IS onset
        `date of certification`                                    IS cert

§§ `Applications`

GIVEN ph   IS A `The policyholder`
      rel  IS A `The insured's relationship to the policyholder`
      dob  IS A DATE
      entry IS A DATE
      term IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The application`
`an application by` ph `for` rel `born` dob `entering on` entry `for a term of` term MEANS
    `The application` WITH
        `the policyholder`                               IS ph
        `the insured's relationship to the policyholder` IS rel
        `written consent of the insured`                 IS TRUE
        `the insured's date of birth`                    IS dob
        `the insured residing in Vietnam`                IS TRUE
        `date of entry into the contract`                IS entry
        `chosen contract term in years`                  IS term

GIVEN dob IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The policyholder`
`an adult resident born` dob MEANS
    `an individual` dob TRUE TRUE

`a company` MEANS `an organisation` TRUE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      pc IS A NUMBER
      living IS A BOOLEAN
      harm IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A beneficiary`
`beneficiary` n `share` pc `alive` living `harmed the insured` harm MEANS
    `A beneficiary` WITH
        `name`                                         IS n
        `designated share, in percent`                 IS pc
        `alive or in existence when the insured event occurred` IS living
        `intentionally harmed the insured`             IS harm
